"body": "<p class=\"note\">All names, numbers and properties in this course are made up for training.</p><div class=\"split\"><div class=\"form\"><div class=\"fhead\"><b>Payoff Statement</b><span>Old Bank, N.A. · Loan Servicing</span></div>\n<table class=\"ft\"><tr><td><span class=\"co\">1</span> Borrower(s)</td><td>Thomas R. Baker, Linda M. Baker</td></tr><tr><td>Property</td><td>412 Maple Ridge Ct, Sampletown, MD 21000</td></tr><tr><td>Loan number</td><td>…7731</td></tr><tr><td>Statement date</td><td>02/20/2027</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"co\">2</span> Good through</td><td>03/12/2027</td></tr></table>\n<h5><span class=\"co\">3</span> Amount to pay in full</h5>\n<table class=\"ft cc\"><tr><td>Unpaid principal balance</td><td>$231,406.18</td></tr><tr><td>Interest from 02/01/2027 to 03/12/2027</td><td>$1,032.66</td></tr><tr><td>Recording / release fee</td><td>$60.00</td></tr><tr><td>Payoff statement fee</td><td>$30.00</td></tr><tr><td>Late charges</td><td>$0.00</td></tr><tr class=\"tot\"><td>Total amount to pay in full by 03/12/2027</td><td>$232,528.84</td></tr></table>\n<table class=\"ft\"><tr><td><span class=\"co\">4</span> Per diem after 03/12/2027</td><td>$25.82 per day</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"co\">5</span> Escrow balance</td><td>$2,184.50 — refunded to borrower separately after payoff</td></tr></table>\n<h5><span class=\"co\">6</span> Remittance</h5>\n<table class=\"ft\"><tr><td>Wire to</td><td>Old Bank, N.A. · ABA ****1102 · Acct ****9035 · Ref: Loan …7731</td></tr><tr><td>Important</td><td>Old Bank will never change wiring instructions by email. Verify by calling the number on our website before sending funds.</td></tr></table>\n<p class=\"fsmall\"><span class=\"co\">7</span> Funds received after 2:00 p.m. ET are credited the next business day. This statement is subject to final verification upon receipt of funds.</p></div><div class=\"expl\"><ol class=\"callouts\"><li><b>Who and what.</b> Borrower names, property address and loan number must match our file and the mortgage listed in the commitment. A payoff for the wrong loan is surprisingly common when the seller has more than one property.</li><li><b>Good-through date.</b> The payoff is only valid through this date. It must be <b>on or after your disbursement date</b>. Closing slipped? Order an updated payoff or add per diem.</li><li><b>The total.</b> Principal plus interest to the good-through date plus fees. This is the number that goes on the settlement statement as the seller's payoff.</li><li><b>Per diem.</b> Daily interest after the good-through date. If the money arrives two days late, add 2 × $25.82, or the payoff will be short and the loan won't be released.</li><li><b>Escrow balance.</b> The servicer refunds the seller's escrow balance <b>after</b> payoff. Don't subtract it from the payoff or credit it on the statement.</li><li><b>Wire instructions.</b> Payoff fraud is real: criminals send fake payoff letters with their own bank account. <b>Call the lender at a phone number you find independently</b> (their website, or a prior verified file) to confirm the instructions before wiring. Never use the number on the letter alone.</li><li><b>Cut-off time.</b> Wires after the cut-off post the next business day, which adds a day of interest. Send payoffs early on disbursement day.</li></ol></div></div>",
