{
"id": "D09",
"s": "DO",
"t": "Surveys and location drawings",
"m": 7,
"body": "<p class=\"note\">All names, numbers and properties in this course are made up for training.</p>\n<p>A survey shows where the property lines are and where the improvements (house, deck, fence, driveway, shed) sit. It's the only way to spot problems that don't appear in the land records.</p>\n<h4>Two kinds</h4>\n<table class=\"lt\"><tr><th></th><th>Location drawing</th><th>Boundary survey</th></tr>\n<tr><td>What it does</td><td>Shows improvements in relation to the lines</td><td>Locates and marks the actual property lines</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Accuracy</td><td>About 1 foot</td><td>Precise</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Typical use</td><td>Most residential purchases</td><td>Commercial, fence disputes, new building, when the buyer wants survey coverage</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Owner's policy survey exception</td><td>Usually stays</td><td>Can be removed</td></tr></table>\n<h4>What to look for</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Encroachments:</b> the neighbor's fence, driveway or shed over the line, or ours over theirs.</li>\n<li><b>Easements:</b> anything built inside a utility or drainage easement.</li>\n<li><b>Building restriction lines (setbacks):</b> the house or an addition past the line on the plat.</li>\n<li><b>Flood zone</b> designation, which may require flood insurance.</li>\n<li>Does the drawing match the <b>legal description and plat</b> in the commitment?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>When you see a problem</h4>\n<p>Don't decide it yourself. Send it to the examiner or underwriter. They may accept it, take a specific exception, ask for an affidavit, or offer affirmative coverage. Tell the agents early so the buyer can decide what to do.</p>",
"keys": [
[
"Location drawing",
"About 1-foot accuracy; survey exception usually stays"
],
[
"Boundary survey",
"Locates lines; can remove survey exception"
],
[
"Look for",
"Encroachments, easements, setbacks, flood zone"
]
],
"traps": [
"A shed in the utility easement can mean the utility has the right to remove it.",
"Underwriting decides how to handle a survey problem. Your job is to catch it and send it up."
],
"qs": [
"PQ36",
"PQ37",
"PQ38"
]
}
